From b53fe0830345f7f1730e4697c8b3b72e08325417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stella Laurenzo <stellaraccident@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:21:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] fix(rocr): honor the build-time hotswap default

Commit d091b08ef0f499de250ce3aac01277a5468c9c56 switched automatic
hotswap loading to opt-in before the integration sequence was ready.
Carry this compatibility patch in TheRock so its builds can restore the
previous default while the upstream sequencing issue is resolved.

Honor HSA_HOTSWAP_DEFAULT_ON when HSA_HOTSWAP_ENABLE is unset. Explicit
environment values, including false and empty values, still take precedence,
preserving the DBT launcher and debugger opt-outs. Builds without the define
retain the opt-in behavior. TheRock supplies the define through its scoped
HSA_HOTSWAP_DEFAULT_ON build flag.

Reproduction: with HSA_HOTSWAP_ENABLE unset on a supported gfx1250 A0
agent, the affected runtime skips automatic hook loading. Building with
HSA_HOTSWAP_DEFAULT_ON=1 restores that path; HSA_HOTSWAP_ENABLE=0
continues to disable it.

Related upstream change:
https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-systems/commit/d091b08ef0f499de250ce3aac01277a5468c9c56
---
 .../rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/util/flag.h     | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/util/flag.h b/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/util/flag.h
index 778f879f5f..4a389578ce 100644
--- a/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/util/flag.h
+++ b/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/util/flag.h
@@ -219,9 +219,13 @@ class Flag {
     var = os::GetEnvVar("HSA_TOOLS_REPORT_REGISTER_FAILURE");
     report_tool_register_failures_ = (var == "1") ? true : false;
 
-    // Opt-in switch for the rocjitsu hotswap tool. Leave the tool disabled
-    // unless the user explicitly requests it with a truthy value.
+    // Explicit environment settings override the build-time hotswap default.
+#if defined(HSA_HOTSWAP_DEFAULT_ON) && HSA_HOTSWAP_DEFAULT_ON
+    hotswap_enable_ = !os::IsEnvVarSet("HSA_HOTSWAP_ENABLE") ||
+        IsEnvVarTruthy("HSA_HOTSWAP_ENABLE");
+#else
     hotswap_enable_ = IsEnvVarTruthy("HSA_HOTSWAP_ENABLE");
+#endif
 
     var = os::GetEnvVar("HSA_DISABLE_FRAGMENT_ALLOCATOR");
     disable_fragment_alloc_ = (var == "1") ? true : false;
